Recommends: nemo, libnotify-bin
Description: Google Drive as a filesystem, streamed, with chosen files kept locally
 OurSync presents Google Drive as an ordinary directory tree, by default at ~/Drive.
 Nothing is downloaded until something reads it, so a Drive far larger than the local
 disk costs nothing to mount, and what has been read is cached and evicted as the cache
 fills. A file that must always be fast, or must survive going offline, is pinned: a real
 copy is placed on local disk, served from there, and never evicted.
 .
 Pinning is what OurSync adds to rclone, whose cache is eviction-based with no way to
 keep a chosen file. A union remote puts a local pin directory in front of the Drive
 remote, so a pinned file is served from disk deterministically, and a write to it
 reaches both copies.
 .
 The mount is read-write when the Drive remote allows it. Changes made through the mount
 reach Drive by themselves; changes made to Drive elsewhere reach a streamed file within
 the poll interval and a pinned file when the refresh timer runs.
 .
 Right-click entries for Nemo are included. Each user runs "oursync setup" once, which
 builds the per-user configuration and walks the one-time Google Cloud step: OurSync
 ships no OAuth client ID, because an application distributing its own client ID with
 Google's restricted drive scope needs OAuth verification and an annual third-party
 security assessment.
